# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Built with [DriftJS](https://github.com/your-org/driftjs) — scaffolded by `driftjs-cli`.

## Getting started

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000.

## Scripts

| Command        | What it does                              |
|----------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `npm run dev`  | Starts the dev server with live reload     |
| `npm run build`| Builds an optimized bundle into `dist/`    |
| `npm run serve`| Serves the built `dist/` folder             |

## Project structure

```
{{PROJECT_NAME}}/
├─ src/
│  ├─ components/   Reusable UI pieces
│  ├─ pages/        Route-level components
│  ├─ assets/       CSS, images, fonts
│  └─ main.js       App entry point
├─ public/          Static files copied as-is
├─ drift.config.js  CLI configuration
└─ package.json
```

## Growing beyond the starter runtime

The scaffold ships with a tiny built-in runtime (`src/drift-runtime.js`) so
your app runs with zero extra installs. As your project grows, swap it for
the full DriftJS package set (compiler, DOM runtime, SSR, Vite plugin) from
the main DriftJS monorepo.
